    thinking: "**Reviewing UI Constraints**\n\nI\'m focusing now on the UI rules, specifically the `frontend-design` and `cloudsql-setup` guidelines, before starting on `src/index.css` and `src/App.tsx`. I\'m especially focused on the UI isolation rule, ensuring no backend details leak into the UI unless explicitly required. This is key to a robust and secure frontend.\n\n\n**Analyzing UI Principles**\n\nI\'m now deep-diving into the `frontend-design` checklist. I\'m nailing down the theme, fonts (`Barlow Condensed`, `Plus Jakarta Sans`, `JetBrains Mono`) and color palette. Also, the critical UI constraints are shaping up: strict avoidance of thick left borders, no pulsing dots, no code-comment headers in the UI, clean unboxed metadata, and single-line controls, all adhering to the minimum height guidelines.\n\n\n**Defining Mobile Navigation**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the mobile experience. I\'ve specified a 15% sticky header and compact bottom navigation bar (`h-14`) for mobile. Google Sign-In is integrated in the header action, storing the ID token for interactive testing.  A \"Sync Now\" button will trigger data fetching, and I\'ve also outlined the structure for weekly picks, a lockout board and dynamic ride-swapping.\n\n\n**Structuring Race Data**\n\nI\'m structuring the race data display. I\'m focusing on three primary tabs. The first tab is \"Race Summary\", showing raw points. The second, \"Live Standings & Matrix Breakdown\", offers filtering and a detailed point matrix, including weekly and season roster breakdowns. The third, \"Driver Bank\", will be filterable by series, showing remaining uses and track history.\n\n\n"
