  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing User Questions**\n\nI\'m focused on understanding the user\'s questions about the app\'s functionality, specifically for league managers and new users. I\'m drawing comparisons to existing fantasy platforms like ESPN and Sleeper to identify existing onboarding procedures, such as a \"league hub\" or \"join\" button, as well as considering other means.\n\n\n**Refining Onboarding Processes**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the invite flow. I envision users signing up, claiming a team (with options for team name, handle, and avatar), then either creating a new league or joining an existing one. A key element is the invite code/link, like `PITBOX-2026`. League managers will then have dedicated controls: a hub to copy the invite link, directly add members, run a draft room, and manage scoring rules.\n\n\n**Adjusting UI Elements**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the UI issues: specifically, spacing and the color palette. The previous layout felt clunky on mobile compared to ESPN and Sleeper. I\'m focusing on high-density, vertical cards, and compact list rows, like Sleeper and ESPN. Also, I\'m analyzing the top NASCAR brand stripe and app header, ensuring it\'s iconic and compact, with the correct colors and placement.\n\n\n**Designing Lineup Interface**\n\nI\'m now detailing the \"My Team/Lineup\" tab, inspired by Sleeper and ESPN. It will feature stacked \"Lineup Slot Rows\" with tap-to-swap functionality, similar to setting fantasy lineups. I\'m planning for weekly starters (Cup, O\'Reilly\'s, Truck) with swap buttons opening bottom sheets showing driver options. Below, there are locked roster slots displaying season-long drivers and car details.\n\n\n**Visualizing Leaderboard Elements**\n\nI\'m now focusing on a compact, expandable leaderboard card design, similar to Sleeper\'s, for each league member. Each card will show weekend and season scores, and tap expansion will reveal the full lineup breakdown: weekly starters and season-long drivers. I\'m also planning the design for the driver bank, inspired by Sleeper, including search and filter functions with easy \"Start\" buttons for weekly lineups. Finally, I\'m working on the draft room interface, also inspired by Sleeper.\n\n\n**Implementing Sign-Up Flow**\n\nI\'m now implementing the sign-up process. I\'m focusing on the \"Join League / Create Team\" functionality. I\'m envisioning an interactive card that allows users to sign up using their name, team name, and an invite code. I\'m also adding Google Sign-In as an option. Backend endpoints are needed for new players to join a league with a team name and invite code, to allow new users to start with a roster immediately. I\'m working on `POST /api/league/join`. I\'m starting by adding the `joinLeagueWithNewTeam` function in the repository.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_11394379658219127758"
      name: "replace_file_content"
      arguments_json: "{\"AllowMultiple\":false, \"Description\":\"Add joinLeagueMember helper to src/db/repository.ts so new users can sign up via Invite Code or Team Name\", \"EndLine\":104, \"Instruction\":\"Add joinLeagueMember function after getOrCreateUser in src/db/repository.ts\", \"ReplacementContent\":\"  } catch (error) {\\n    console.error(\'Database error in getOrCreateUser:\', error);\\n    throw new Error(\'Failed to synchronize user profile.\', { cause: error });\\n  }\\n}\\n\\nexport async function joinLeagueMember(params: {\\n  name: string;\\n  email?: string;\\n  avatar?: string;\\n  inviteCode?: string;\\n}) {\\n  try {\\n    const cleanName = params.name.trim();\\n    if (!cleanName) {\\n      throw new Error(\'Please enter your Manager or Team Name.\');\\n    }\\n\\n    const allUsers = await db.select().from(users);\\n    const nextRank = allUsers.length + 1;\\n    const newId = `u_${Date.now().toString(36)}`;\\n    const initials =\\n      params.avatar?.trim().toUpperCase().slice(0, 2) ||\\n      cleanName\\n        .split(\' \')\\n        .map((w) => w[0])\\n        .join(\'\')\\n        .toUpperCase()\\n        .slice(0, 2) ||\\n      \'NP\';\\n\\n    const insertedUser = await db\\n      .insert(users)\\n      .values({\\n        id: newId,\\n        uid: `invite_${newId}`,\\n        email:\\n          params.email?.trim() ||\\n          `${cleanName.toLowerCase().replace(/[^a-z0-9]/g, \'\')}@pitboxfantasy.com`,\\n        name: cleanName,\\n        avatar: initials,\\n        lastYearRank: nextRank,\\n        role: \'member\',\\n        cumulativePriorPoints: 2300,\\n      })\\n      .returning();\\n\\n    // Auto-assign open undrafted season drivers if available so the new manager has a working lineup\\n    const allRosters = await db.select().from(seasonRosters);\\n    const allDrivers = await db.select().from(drivers);\\n    const takenIds = new Set(\\n      allRosters\\n        .filter((r) => r.slotType !== \'cup_current_chase\')\\n        .map((r) => r.driverId)\\n    );\\n\\n    const pickOpenDriver = (\\n      sId: number,\\n      filterFn: (d: typeof allDrivers[0]) => boolean,\\n      fallbackId: string\\n    ) => {\\n      const found = allDrivers.find(\\n        (d) =>\\n          d.seriesId === sId &&\\n          !d.isBuschwhacker &&\\n          !takenIds.has(d.id) &&\\n          filterFn(d)\\n      );\\n      return found || allDrivers.find((d) => d.id === fallbackId)!;\\n    };\\n\\n    const cupChaseDrv = pickOpenDriver(1, (d) => d.madeLastYearChase, \'c7\');\\n    takenIds.add(cupChaseDrv.id);\\n    const cupNonChaseDrv = pickOpenDriver(\\n      1,\\n      (d) => !d.madeLastYearChase,\\n      \'cn7\'\\n    );\\n    takenIds.add(cupNonChaseDrv.id);\\n    const oreillyDrv = pickOpenDriver(2, () => true, \'o7\');\\n    takenIds.add(oreillyDrv.id);\\n    const truckDrv = pickOpenDriver(3, () => true, \'t7\');\\n    takenIds.add(truckDrv.id);\\n\\n    const starterSlots = [\\n      {\\n        seriesId: 1,\\n        slotType: \'cup_prev_chase\',\\n        driverId: cupChaseDrv.id,\\n        fallbackCarNumber: cupChaseDrv.carNumber,\\n      },\\n      {\\n        seriesId: 1,\\n        slotType: \'cup_prev_non_chase\',\\n        driverId: cupNonChaseDrv.id,\\n        fallbackCarNumber: cupNonChaseDrv.carNumber,\\n      },\\n      {\\n        seriesId: 2,\\n        slotType: \'oreillys_season\',\\n        driverId: oreillyDrv.id,\\n        fallbackCarNumber: oreillyDrv.carNumber,\\n      },\\n      {\\n        seriesId: 3,\\n        slotType: \'trucks_season\',\\n        driverId: truckDrv.id,\\n        fallbackCarNumber: truckDrv.carNumber,\\n      },\\n      {\\n        seriesId: 1,\\n        slotType: \'cup_current_chase\',\\n        driverId: \'c1\',\\n        fallbackCarNumber: \'5\',\\n      },\\n    ];\\n\\n    for (const s of starterSlots) {\\n      await db\\n        .insert(seasonRosters)\\n        .values({\\n          userId: newId,\\n          seriesId: s.seriesId,\\n          slotType: s.slotType,\\n          driverId: s.driverId,\\n          fallbackCarNumber: s.fallbackCarNumber,\\n        })\\n        .onConflictDoNothing();\\n    }\\n\\n    // Assign default weekly picks for the active weekend\\n    const defaultWeekly = [\\n      { raceId: \'r_cup_bristol\', seriesId: 1, driverId: cupChaseDrv.id },\\n      { raceId: \'r_oreillys_bristol\', seriesId: 2, driverId: \'o_bw1\' },\\n      { raceId: \'r_trucks_bristol\', seriesId: 3, driverId: \'t_bw1\' },\\n    ];\\n\\n    for (const wp of defaultWeekly) {\\n      await db\\n        .insert(weeklyPicks)\\n        .values({\\n          userId: newId,\\n          raceId: wp.raceId,\\n          seriesId: wp.seriesId,\\n          driverId: wp.driverId,\\n          trackLabel: \'Bristol Night\',\\n          isHistorical: false,\\n        })\\n        .onConflictDoNothing();\\n    }\\n\\n    return insertedUser[0];\\n  } catch (error) {\\n    throw new Error(\\n      error instanceof Error ? error.message : \'Failed to join league.\',\\n      { cause: error }\\n    );\\n  }\\n}\", \"StartLine\":99, \"TargetContent\":\"  } catch (error) {\\n    console.error(\'Database error in getOrCreateUser:\', error);\\n    throw new Error(\'Failed to synchronize user profile.\', { cause: error });\\n  }\\n}\", \"TargetFile\":\"/src/db/repository.ts\", \"toolAction\":\"Adding joinLeagueMember to src/db/repository.ts\", \"toolSummary\":\"Add joinLeagueMember to repository\"}"
